This project demonstrates a Python-based simulator for testing MQTT communication behavior in an IoT device.

The project focuses on connection handling, message publishing, subscription behavior, communication interruptions, reconnection, and recovery scenarios.

Testing Covered
MQTT connection testing
Publish testing
Subscribe testing
Disconnect testing
Reconnection testing
Recovery testing
Negative testing
PASS/FAIL validation
CSV test reporting
Test Scenarios
Test ID	Scenario	Expected
TC001	MQTT connection	PASS
TC002	Publish message	PASS
TC003	Subscribe to topic	PASS
TC004	Disconnect device	PASS
TC005	Publish while disconnected	FAIL
TC006	Reconnect to MQTT	PASS
TC007	Publish after reconnection	PASS
Technologies
Python
MQTT concepts
IoT communication
QA test scenarios
CSV reporting
Purpose

The project demonstrates how communication interruptions and recovery behavior can be represented in an embedded/IoT testing workflow.

The simulator is software-based and is intended to demonstrate testing concepts rather than replace testing on a physical MQTT device.
  
